      "caption": "‼️‼️Watch The Progress Update at the End ‼️‼️\n\n💥Love to See Players Growing and Developing into Their Mechanics as they mature! 🙌🙌\n\n✅This Video was posted over a year ago and to see the progress in his development is awesome. This is what consistency is all about. \n\n✅Learning proper mechanics at a young age is great because as the player starts to grow into their body they start to move more efficiently! \n\n@aamena_29 \n\n📲For private lessons or Remote training Dm me \n\n#pitchingmechanics #pitchingtraining #baseballcoach #pitchingdrills #santiagosoldiers",
      "transcript": "So that means your first initial move wants to go diving down. That's why you'll see that knee go here and keep going forward because all that weight is coming from up here. All that weight is coming this way. You want the opposite. You want the weight coming from here. This I'm saying over exaggerate, keeping the head back while your legs are going forward. Here your body has time to rotate, rotate, rotate and then finish over your front leg. I feel like you're stretching that foot forward. All I'm doing is reaching with my foot. To that point now if I wanted to from here, I can go ahead and throw. I got my weight back, all my power, my energy is stored. Now I'm just rotating to throw. How's that feel? Good. That looked amazing. That was awesome.",
